import QualityLayout from "../../../layouts/QualityLayout.astro";
---

<QualityLayout
  title="Feedback and review — Counterfact quality study"
  description="How to review, question, or correct the Counterfact quality study and its public evidence."
  canonicalPath="/quality/2026/feedback"
  active="feedback"
>
  <article class="appendix-page quality-reading quality-prose">
    <header class="appendix-header">
      <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/quality/2026">Article</a> / Review the study</p>
      <h1>Feedback and review</h1>
      <p>
        This study publishes source-linked records, calculations, and methods for public scrutiny. It invites corrections, alternative interpretations, and improvements to its methods.
      </p>
    </header>



    <section class="authorship-disclosure" aria-labelledby="authorship-heading">
      <h2 id="authorship-heading">Authorship and scrutiny</h2>
      <p>
        Codex authored this evaluation at the request of Counterfact maintainer Patrick McElhaney. Patrick commissioned the review and decided to publish it; Codex performed the repository evaluation and drafted the report.
      </p>
      <p>
        Codex also participated in the agent-assisted work under evaluation. That circularity does not make the conclusions independent. Readers can instead assess the safeguards: source-linked records, published calculations and methods, reproducible experiments, visible unresolved records, and a public path for correction.
      </p>
      <p>
        The purpose of publication is to make the evidence and methods available for scrutiny, alternative interpretations, and learning. A correction supported by the record should change the report.
      </p>
    </section>

    <h2>What to review</h2>
    <p>
      Start with the <a href="/quality/2026/candidates#original-ledger">detailed external-report cases</a>
      {" "}and the <a href="/quality/2026/candidates#census">public-record census</a>. The <a href="/quality/2026/cases">case records</a>,
      {" "}<a href="/quality/2026/experiments">verification experiments</a>,
      {" "}<a href="/quality/2026/methodology">data and methods</a>, and
      {" "}<a href="/quality/2026/data.json">Download data</a> provide the
      corresponding source and calculation record.
    </p>

    <h2>Review standard</h2>
    <p>
      A helpful review identifies the challenged claim and links it to the
      relevant public source, such as an issue, pull request, commit, release,
      or coverage result. If the evidence supports a different
      interpretation, the report should be corrected rather than defended.
    </p>
    <h2>How to respond</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:pmcelhaney@gmail.com">pmcelhaney@gmail.com</a> for
      feedback, questions, or corrections. Because the source lives in the
      Counterfact repository, readers may also open a
      {" "}<a href="https://github.com/counterfact/api-simulator/issues/new">GitHub issue</a>{" "}
      or submit a
      {" "}<a href="https://github.com/counterfact/api-simulator/compare">pull request</a>{" "}
      with a proposed correction.
    </p>
  </article>
</QualityLayout>
